  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "When something happens",
     "texto": [
      "Before **때** («time/moment»), a form is used that depends on tense. For a present or habitual situation: **-(으)ㄹ 때** with verbs (**갈 때**, when I go; **먹을 때**, when I eat) and adjectives (**바쁠 때**, when I'm busy). For a past situation: **-았/었을 때** (**한국에 갔을 때**, when I went to Korea)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "A common expression",
     "texto": [
      "**어렸을 때** means «when I was little»: 어리다 → 어렸을 때. The form before 때 gives the time relationship; it does not always mean the future, even though it contains ㄹ. To ask «when?» use **언제**: 언제 만날 거예요? = When will we meet?"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Verb or adjective",
     "columnas": [
